From f9bd5ecbdb62c9b24f8d13e62baf1a0484732647 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 12:47:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] PBR: map the Wii Remote to the handheld, and ship a starter
 save

PBR launched with NO working controls: the auto-mapper only ever knew
GameCube and GBA pads, so the emulated Wii Remote was left unbound and
the touch overlay was the only input -- and on this hardware the
touchscreen makes an unreliable pointer. Map Wiimote 1 alongside the
other pads: face buttons to A/B/1/2/+/-, D-pad straight through, and the
POINTER ON THE RIGHT STICK (Dolphin's cursor group takes ordinary axis
bindings), which aims far better than touch on a handheld. The overlay
stays on as a backup. '+' prefers Start and only falls back to Menu when
Start is absent, so it can never share a button with HOME.

Also fix the chicken-and-egg that made the PBR team editor unusable: the
editor needs a save, but PBR only writes one after you have played it
(and, for online, connected once). Bundle a community starter save --
all four profiles storage-unlocked -- and install it when the user has
none. It ships decrypted and gzipped (551 KB; the encrypted form does
not compress at all) and is re-encrypted at install through the same
cipher the editor already round-trips byte-identically, then loaded back
to prove what was written parses. An existing save is NEVER overwritten,
and there is a picker for anyone bringing their own file, which is
validated by parsing it and backs up whatever was there.

The save is filed under the title directory matching the DETECTED disc,
not always the USA one: a PAL player's save would otherwise land where
their game never looks, and the checklist would call it installed.
Seeding runs off the UI thread (3.5 MB of gunzip + encrypt + verify),
writes land atomically with the rename result actually checked, and a
missing gamepad can no longer throw out of the checklist refresh.

Credit: the bundled save is the community "Restorer Forever" save from
Project Pokemon (file 5057).
